who reads decides what unfolds. a word is jargon only against a reader
who lacks it — shorthand to a peer, a wall to a junior. the sentence is
the same either way.

the question names the reader. why/how — unfold each term at first use.
what/where — name it and move on.

default, where nothing names one: a competent developer of the trade who
has never seen this tree. they know http, sql, a form framework, an orm.
they do not know what we called things — `general/jargon`.
